mill-proof.logic.r3: argue/answered: U1: answered yes, which keeps mill-proof.logic.r3, to: Does the text's argument take this for granted, whether or not it says so: "if the general happiness is a good to the aggregate of all persons, then happiness has made out its title as one of the ends of conduct"? Answer yes if the author would accept it as part of the argument.
